  "_what": "The files every sign-in page names (src/account/sign_in/assets.rs): the brand mark, the tab and home-screen icons, the manifest, the page look's stylesheet and its fonts. Each file has its content identity (`identity`, `1f:` + BLAKE3 hex of the bytes, the Namespace's own form). A computer serves a file from its verified content cache (`<accounts>/content/<identity>`, the same bytes at `/content/<identity>`), and falls back to `file` under the look's `static_root` until the bytes are uploaded and verified on two places. Only these identities are served at `/content/`: this list is the allow-list. `origins` are the https holders a computer fetches a missing file from, once, in order (`/content/<identity>` on each); `fetch` bounds one answer. The forwarder carries each path whole and `/content/<identity>` (src/forwarder/new_accounts.json `carried_paths` and `content_prefix`).",
